<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01264#mapping_id_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'you're a special kinda nuts' is mapped onto the visual entity 'squirrel', using the pun on the word 'nuts' — referring to the animal's natural behavior of storing nuts, which is humorously equated with being crazy or eccentric. The squirrel's alert and curious expression reinforces the playful, 'nuts' stereotype, creating an analogical mapping between the textual pun and the visual representation of the animal."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#geometricallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:n4c986ac4ba6c41688210d6715d29faa3b37 .
