<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01264#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the squirrel, as the text 'you're a special kinda nuts' directly addresses the viewer ('you') and implies that the viewer (or the squirrel, as a stand-in) is 'nuts'. The rhetorical question 'aren't you?' further reinforces this projection by inviting the user to identify with the subject of the pun. The squirrel serves as the visual entity onto which the user is projected, through the pun and the direct address in the text."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DimensionsInterrelation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
